    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §2, Chap 137 of 1877",
    "lawSection": "Port Chester, Village of",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S4130\n\nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend chapter 137 of the laws of 1877 relating to\nincorporating the library and reading room of the village of Port\nChester in Westchester county, in relation to a free association\nlibrary\n\nPURPOSE:\n\nThis legislation clarifies in state law that the Port Chester Rye\nBrook Public Library is a free association library\n\nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nThis legislation amends Section 2 of chapter 137 of the laws of 1877\nrelating to incorporating the library and reading room of the village\nof Port Chester in Westchester county to make clear that the Port\nChester Rye Brook Public Library is a free association library as it\nhas been operated as such throughout it's history.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation has been requested by the library's Board of Trustees\nto memorialize the library's status as a free association library. The\nlibrary has functioned in this manner throughout the history of the\ninstitution. The library has not been previously treated as a\nmunicipal library or department of local government by the villages of\nPort Chester or Rye Brook. The library has selected board in a manner\nconsistent with an association library. This legislation is intended\nto clarify this status of the library. The library is funded with\nmunicipal contributions, revenues and private donations in a manner\nconsistent with it's status as an association library\n\nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew legislation\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the state.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\n\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n\n",
